1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,174
This is a boarding party.

2
00:00:03,074 --> 00:00:06,552
This was the Helm console a minute ago,

3
00:00:07,002 --> 00:00:12,220
and now it's the handheld of someone who has left the ship.

4
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:16,628
They're standing on a landing field,

5
00:00:17,078 --> 00:00:20,991
talking to a woman who says everything is fine.

6
00:00:22,791 --> 00:00:25,400
Nobody drew this place. It's this:

7
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:28,459
about a hundred lines of text.

8
00:00:30,259 --> 00:00:33,737
In this class, you write places like it.

9
00:00:34,187 --> 00:00:37,665
Today, you play one that somebody else wrote,

10
00:00:38,115 --> 00:00:41,593
and then you read how it was made.

11
00:00:42,793 --> 00:00:44,533
First, a new mission.

12
00:00:45,433 --> 00:00:49,780
This class doesn't build on the one from Class 1.

13
00:00:50,230 --> 00:00:53,709
That story ends the game ten minutes in,

14
00:00:54,159 --> 00:00:58,941
and a boarding party should be allowed to take its time.

15
00:01:00,741 --> 00:01:05,089
So I make a mission the way I did before,

16
00:01:05,539 --> 00:01:08,148
and I call it My Boarding.

17
00:01:09,048 --> 00:01:12,526
Then I bring its libraries up to date,

18
00:01:12,976 --> 00:01:16,889
open the folder in the editor, and run lint.

19
00:01:17,789 --> 00:01:23,441
It's clean, and it's the same small mission you started Class 1 with.

20
00:01:24,641 --> 00:01:29,859
There's a shipped campaign with a colony in it called Ferrow Landing.

21
00:01:30,759 --> 00:01:33,802
Eleven people, a raked gravel landing field,

22
00:01:34,252 --> 00:01:37,730
and an administrator with an answer for everything.

23
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:43,009
On the handheld, the bar names the room,

24
00:01:43,459 --> 00:01:47,372
and everything under it, the line and the buttons,

25
00:01:47,822 --> 00:01:51,300
comes from the block I'm about to paste.

26
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:57,448
I go to the very end of my fact sheet,

27
00:01:57,898 --> 00:02:00,507
and I paste that colony's scene.

28
00:02:01,407 --> 00:02:03,146
Don't read it yet.

29
00:02:04,946 --> 00:02:07,554
Lint has one thing to say.

30
00:02:08,004 --> 00:02:12,352
Nothing in this mission reads these rooms. And that's true,

31
00:02:12,802 --> 00:02:16,280
because a scene needs something to start it.

32
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:22,428
On Helm, the handheld icon opens a page of tiles,

33
00:02:22,878 --> 00:02:27,661
and one called Boarding Party offers the visit by its name.

34
00:02:28,561 --> 00:02:33,778
That name, and the moment the tile appears, are on a card.

35
00:02:34,678 --> 00:02:39,461
So I open the story file, go to the very end,

36
00:02:39,911 --> 00:02:41,650
and paste the card.

37
00:02:42,550 --> 00:02:44,289
Now lint is clean.

38
00:02:45,489 --> 00:02:50,272
I start the game with a server and a Helm console,

39
00:02:50,722 --> 00:02:53,330
and I fly toward the hulk.

40
00:02:54,230 --> 00:02:57,274
When I'm close, I stop the ship,

41
00:02:57,724 --> 00:02:59,898
and I open the handheld.

42
00:03:01,698 --> 00:03:07,785
There's a tile called Boarding Party, and it's offering Ferrow Landing. I beam down.

43
00:03:09,585 --> 00:03:12,193
Now this console is my handheld.

44
00:03:13,093 --> 00:03:15,702
Two of these buttons are plain.

45
00:03:16,152 --> 00:03:17,891
The others say covering,

46
00:03:18,341 --> 00:03:20,080
and then a job.

47
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:24,024
Those belong to people who aren't here,

48
00:03:24,474 --> 00:03:30,561
and I'm one helm officer, so they all come to me. I take one,

49
00:03:31,011 --> 00:03:35,793
and I read what a medic would've noticed. I walk in.

50
00:03:36,243 --> 00:03:38,417
I ask about the cable.

51
00:03:39,317 --> 00:03:41,926
And she won't open the shed,

52
00:03:42,376 --> 00:03:46,289
because I haven't found enough to say out loud.

53
00:03:48,089 --> 00:03:51,133
So I go back and look harder.

54
00:03:52,033 --> 00:03:53,772
Three things found out,

55
00:03:54,222 --> 00:03:56,396
and now the button's there.

56
00:03:57,596 --> 00:03:59,335
Now let's read it.

57
00:04:00,235 --> 00:04:03,713
Here's the landing field on the handheld again:

58
00:04:04,163 --> 00:04:08,946
the room's name in the bar, one line, and six buttons.

59
00:04:10,746 --> 00:04:15,528
In the file, it's one section, with fourteen records in it,

60
00:04:15,978 --> 00:04:18,587
and each record is a room.

61
00:04:20,387 --> 00:04:23,430
A room has no fence at all.

62
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:28,678
These lines, the ones that start with a percent sign,

63
00:04:29,128 --> 00:04:31,302
are what the party finds.

64
00:04:32,202 --> 00:04:33,941
There are two here,

65
00:04:34,391 --> 00:04:37,870
and the game showed me one of them.

66
00:04:39,670 --> 00:04:43,148
Each line with a dash is a choice.

67
00:04:43,598 --> 00:04:46,207
The words go on a button,

68
00:04:46,657 --> 00:04:51,874
and the key in round brackets is the room it leads to.

69
00:04:53,674 --> 00:04:55,848
This one adds a condition.

70
00:04:56,298 --> 00:04:58,907
Only a medic is offered it.

71
00:04:59,807 --> 00:05:05,893
I'm not a medic, so it came to me marked as covering for medical.

72
00:05:06,793 --> 00:05:08,533
And after the semicolon,

73
00:05:08,983 --> 00:05:10,722
the party learns something.

74
00:05:12,522 --> 00:05:16,870
At the cable, the handheld had no Open it button,

75
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:19,493
until I'd found three things.

76
00:05:20,393 --> 00:05:23,002
Here's that door in the file.

77
00:05:23,452 --> 00:05:27,365
It asks how many things the party has learned.

78
00:05:29,165 --> 00:05:34,383
And this last kind has nothing in its brackets. It leads nowhere,

79
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:37,007
and it ends the visit.

80
00:05:37,907 --> 00:05:41,820
On the handheld, it's the Beam back up button.

81
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:46,498
The shipped file is about two hundred lines,

82
00:05:46,948 --> 00:05:49,557
and I pasted half of it.

83
00:05:51,357 --> 00:05:57,443
It opens with a page of notes, from the author to whoever comes next.

84
00:05:58,343 --> 00:06:03,996
This one says every room has to lead back as well as on,

85
00:06:04,446 --> 00:06:08,359
and it says so because the first version didn't.

86
00:06:10,159 --> 00:06:11,898
Then there's a voice,

87
00:06:12,348 --> 00:06:16,696
the administrator, of the kind you'll meet in Class 2.

88
00:06:17,596 --> 00:06:22,378
And there's the call that starts the scene in that campaign,

89
00:06:22,828 --> 00:06:27,176
when the ship docks at the colony. I cut those,

90
00:06:27,626 --> 00:06:32,409
and the table on the page says what went and why.

91
00:06:33,609 --> 00:06:38,391
Ferrow Landing was a loan, so now I give it back.

92
00:06:39,291 --> 00:06:45,378
In the fact sheet I delete everything from the Scenes heading to the end,

93
00:06:45,828 --> 00:06:48,002
and it's sixty lines again.

94
00:06:48,902 --> 00:06:52,380
In the story file I delete the card,

95
00:06:52,830 --> 00:06:55,439
and that's a hundred and five.

96
00:06:57,239 --> 00:07:01,152
I save both, I run lint, and it's clean.

97
00:07:02,052 --> 00:07:05,530
Don't leave the card behind. Lint won't mind,

98
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:11,198
but the game will go looking for a room that isn't there.

99
00:07:12,398 --> 00:07:15,441
Before you delete it, play with it.

100
00:07:16,341 --> 00:07:18,950
Change the name on the card,

101
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:22,009
and find it on the tile.

102
00:07:22,909 --> 00:07:25,952
Make the shed ask for five things,

103
00:07:26,402 --> 00:07:29,880
and see how much harder the colony gets.

104
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:35,159
Then answer three questions from the file alone,

105
00:07:35,609 --> 00:07:37,348
with the game closed.

106
00:07:39,148 --> 00:07:43,061
Next time, you write a place of your own:

107
00:07:43,511 --> 00:07:45,250
a crew, three rooms,

108
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:48,309
and the card that starts it.
